  "Question": "\\(\\angle AOB=100^\\circ\\), ray OC lies in the interior of \\(\\angle AOB\\), and \\(\\angle AOC=3\\angle BOC\\). What is the measure of \\(\\angle BOC\\), in degrees?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "25",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let \\(\\angle BOC=x\\). Then \\(\\angle AOC=3x\\), so \\(x+3x=100^\\circ\\). Solving gives \\(x=25^\\circ\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Divide into equal parts\n\nBecause \\(OC\\) lies inside \\(\\angle AOB\\), the two smaller angles together measure \\(100^\\circ\\). The angle \\(\\angle AOC\\) contains three parts of the size of \\(\\angle BOC\\), so the whole angle contains four equal parts. Therefore\n\\[\n\\angle BOC=100^\\circ\\div(3+1)=25^\\circ.\n\\]",
